confirmed.fix:
Add a global guard in `internal/hud/frontend/src/lib/styles/theme.css` (near the existing @keyframes block ~L405):

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.001ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.001ms !important;
    scroll-behavior: auto !important;
  }
}
```

For semantically-meaningful indicators (offline status dot, claim-conflict chip, Mills banner-pulse, LabsAccessBar) where motion conveys state, prefer the inverse pattern so they degrade to a static high-contrast style instead of disappearing entirely. Example for `App.svelte:858`:

```css
.status-indicator.offline {
  background: var(--status-offline);
  box-shadow: 0 0 4px var(--status-offline);
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .status-indicator.offline { animation: pulse 1.5s infinite; }
}
```

Apply the same no-preference wrapper at the named offenders: OverlayShell.svelte:550, LiveSessionsCard.svelte:419, fleet/ClaimConflictChip.svelte:155, shared/LabsAccessBar.svelte:190, Mills/OverviewPanel.svelte:493/499, theme.css `.status-breathe` (L422-424), and `.skeleton` shimmer (L453-463). Then `make hud-frontend`, commit the rebuilt `dist/` (it's go:embed'd), and verify with `grep prefers-reduced-motion internal/hud/frontend/dist/assets/index-*.css`.

